          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "To automate order intake, shop-floor data capture, and operational workflows without replacing your core ERP (often Pronto, Epicor, SYSPRO, SAP Business One, or Greentree), you need a partner that excels in **hybrid integration, custom connectors, and rugged low-code UX**. \n\nA successful \"wrap-and-extend\" approach requires a consultant who treats your ERP as the transactional system of record while using **Microsoft Power Platform (Power Apps, Power Automate, AI Builder) and Azure** as the agile layer for frontline workers.\n\nConsultancies with a presence in Brisbane or Australia that fit this specific brief include:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Dedicated Business Applications & Power Platform Specialists\n* **Barhead Solutions (an Akkodis company)**\n  * **Brisbane Presence:** Office located in Brisbane CBD (Queen St).\n  * **Why them:** They are one of Australia’s premier Microsoft Solutions Partners dedicated specifically to Power Platform, Dynamics, and AI solutions. They excel at architecting Power Platform Centers of Excellence (CoE), custom connectors, and extending legacy architectures without rip-and-replace.\n  * **Fit:** Medium to enterprise manufacturers that want rigorous architecture, governance, and enterprise-grade integration.\n\n* **Inturing**\n  * **Presence:** Australian specialist consultancy.\n  * **Why them:** A boutique consultancy whose core marketing and capability directly target **operational Australian manufacturers**. They build purpose-built shop-floor Power Apps (downtime tracking, quality inspections, digital job cards) and workflow automations that sit on top of existing business systems.\n  * **Fit:** Manufacturers looking for a lean, agile partner who speaks manufacturing terminology (BOMs, routings, batch tracking, OEE) rather than just generic IT.\n\n* **Fusion5**\n  * **Brisbane Presence:** Dedicated Brisbane office / Queensland team.\n  * **Why them:** Uniquely positioned because they are both a major ERP partner (Dynamics, NetSuite) and a modern Microsoft Cloud & Power Platform solutions provider. Because they live and breathe ERP implementations, their integration architects understand how ERP databases, lockups, and APIs behave when queried by external low-code applications.\n  * **Fit:** If your ERP is a mid-market system and you want an integrator who understands backend ERP accounting and stock constraints.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Brisbane-Headquartered & Local Specialist Teams\n* **Data#3**\n  * **Brisbane Presence:** Global Headquarters in Brisbane (Toowong).\n  * **Why them:** As one of Australia's largest Microsoft Partners, they are best suited if your operational overhaul also touches IT governance, cybersecurity (Essential Eight), hybrid networking (connecting on-premises factory networks to cloud APIs), and Azure infrastructure.\n  * **Fit:** Larger industrial facilities with strict IT/OT security and compliance mandates.\n\n* **C9 Solutions / Team 400**\n  * **Brisbane Presence:** Local development teams in Brisbane.\n  * **Why them:** Specialized in rapid low-code/pro-code application engineering, AI Builder (for automated document/order extraction), and custom connectors. \n  * **Fit:** Quick proofs-of-concept (POCs) for order intake processing and specific mobile app builds.\n\n---\n\n### Key Technical Criteria to Vet When You Speak With Them\n\nBefore engaging any partner, ensure they can solve the practical challenges specific to manufacturing:\n\n1. **How will they connect to your specific ERP?**\n   * *Direct APIs vs. On-Premises Data Gateway vs. Webhooks:* If your ERP doesn’t have open REST APIs, the partner should have experience building custom Azure connectors or using the **On-Premises Data Gateway** for direct SQL/ODBC reads and staging tables to avoid locking tables during production.\n2. **Shop Floor Device & Environmental UX:**\n   * Power Apps on the shop floor must accommodate barcode scanning (Honeywell/Zebra handhelds or camera OCR), glove use, high-contrast screens, and **offline caching** for when Wi-Fi drops out in steel-framed factory sheds.\n3. **Automated Order Processing (OCR & AI):**\n   * Ask how they handle unstructured PDF customer purchase orders. The gold standard right now involves **Power Automate + AI Builder (Document Processing models) or Azure OpenAI** to parse inbound PDFs, extract line items, match customer parts to internal SKUs, and post draft sales orders directly into your ERP for review.\n4. **Licensing & Multiplexing Compliance:**\n   * A shop floor of 50–200 workers can quickly drive up software costs if improperly licensed. Ask how they design the architecture to comply with **Microsoft Multiplexing rules** and ERP user licensing while keeping per-user/per-app subscription costs sustainable.\n\n### Recommended Next Step\nReach out to **Barhead Solutions** (for enterprise-level Power Platform architecture) and **Fusion5** or a boutique manufacturing specialist like **Inturing**. Request a brief discovery session focused on a **single pilot project**—such as *automating PDF sales order entry* or *a tablet-based shop-floor job-tracking app*—to validate their integration capability before scoping the broader operations.",
              "thoughtSignature": ""
            }
          ],
